  "verbalization": "Mirtazapine is associated with Anxiety Disorder through a chain of indications that link it to Endogenous Depression, which in turn is indicated for multiple drugs including Trazodone, Levomilnacipran, and Gepirone. These drugs are all known to have antianxiety properties, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of neurotransmitter systems, particularly those related to serotonin and GABA. The shared indication of Endogenous Depression across these drugs implies a common pathway or target, possibly involving the regulation of mood and anxiety-related neural circuits. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Mirtazapine may exert its antianxiety effects through a mechanism that is indirectly linked to these other drugs, potentially by influencing similar biological pathways or by acting on overlapping targets. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering the broader pharmacological context when evaluating the potential of Mirtazapine for the treatment of anxiety disorders."
